message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived software record and the associated article when available."
title: "Code for Global phytoplankton responses to spatiotemporally continuous marine heatwaves and cold spells"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Ren
    given-names: Jie
    affiliation: "Laboratory of Tropical Oceanography, South China Sea Institute of Oceanology, Chinese Academy of Sciences"
  - family-names: Yao
    given-names: Yulong
    affiliation: "Laboratory of Tropical Oceanography, South China Sea Institute of Oceanology, Chinese Academy of Sciences"
  - family-names: Wang
    given-names: Chunzai
    affiliation: "South China Sea Institute of Oceanology, Chinese Academy of Sciences"
abstract: >-
  Code for the main-text figures of a study of global chlorophyll-a,
  model-derived phytoplankton size-class, and mixed-layer-depth responses to
  spatiotemporally continuous marine heatwaves and cold spells during
  2001–2023. The archive contains the plotting and figure-assembly scripts
  for Figures 1–6; the upstream event-detection and clustering pipeline, the
  supplementary-figure code, and all input data are not included.
keywords:
  - marine heatwaves
  - marine cold spells
  - chlorophyll-a
  - phytoplankton size classes
  - mixed-layer depth
  - spatiotemporal clustering
  - DBSCAN
  - remote sensing
